---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import siteConfig from "../data/site.config.json";
import { breadcrumbListJsonLd } from "../lib/schema";

const siteUrl = `https://${siteConfig.domain}`;
const title = `About ${siteConfig.siteName} - independent UK carp gear reviews`;
const description = `Who we are, how we test, and why we take no manufacturer sponsorship. Independent carp fishing gear reviews for UK anglers.`;

const jsonLd = breadcrumbListJsonLd([
  { label: "Home", url: `${siteUrl}/` },
  { label: "About", url: `${siteUrl}/about/` },
]);
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  indexable={true}
  crumbs={[{ label: "About" }]}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="guide-content">
      <div class="page-head">
        <div class="kicker">About</div>
        <h1>About {siteConfig.siteName}</h1>
        <p class="lede">Independent carp fishing gear reviews for UK anglers. No sponsorship, no free kit from manufacturers, no rankings shaped by commission rates.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
      <p>
        Most UK carp fishing content online is either written by tackle-shop staff whose job is to move stock, or by sponsored anglers whose
        rod bag came free. Both produce useful content and both have a bias. We started {siteConfig.siteName} because it was hard to find
        honest opinions on kit we were paying real money for, and because "best bivvy 2025" articles that recommend the same seven brands
        as every other article are not helping anyone decide.
      </p>

      <h2>How we test and rate</h2>
      <p>
        Every product we review at four stars or above is one we would put our own money on. Ratings are editorial and reflect long-term
        performance, not opening-day impressions. We rate kit against realistic UK use - a bivvy is tested in November rain, not summer
        campsite conditions; alarms are judged on how they behave with 300 m of braid in the wind, not on a test bench.
      </p>
      <p>
        We accept that we cannot test every product long-term ourselves. Where we haven't put ten sessions into a piece of kit, we say so -
        our summary either flags the review as based on published specs and community consensus, or the product does not appear on the site.
      </p>

      <h2>How we make money</h2>
      <p>
        Every product page and every guide on this site carries Amazon UK affiliate links. When a reader buys through one of those links,
        Amazon pays us a small commission (typically 3% on Sports & Outdoors category items, capped at £7 per item). This costs the reader
        nothing extra. It is our only source of income.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because Amazon pays the same commission regardless of which brand is bought, we have no reason to push one manufacturer over another.
        We recommend what we would buy. If a product is priced better on a specialist retailer (Angling Direct, Nash Direct, Trakker UK
        website), we say so - we lose the sale but keep the trust.
      </p>
      <p>
        Full details of our commercial relationships are on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Who writes this</h2>
      <p>
        {siteConfig.siteName} is run by a small editorial desk of UK carp anglers with combined experience across syndicate waters, big-pit
        day-ticket venues, and specimen fishing. Editorial decisions are made on kit, not on which brand happens to be currently promoting.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections and disagreements</h2>
      <p>
        We get things wrong. If a review misrepresents a product, or if a specification is out of date because a manufacturer has changed a
        blank or a pole material, please <a href="/contact/">send us a message</a>. We correct
        openly, dated, and named at the bottom of the affected page.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not accept manufacturer sponsorship.</li>
        <li>We do not accept free product for review.</li>
        <li>We do not run "sponsored posts" of any kind.</li>
        <li>We do not use AI to generate product reviews - writing is done by humans who have handled or owned the kit.</li>
        <li>We do not track visitors beyond basic anonymised traffic analytics. See <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>The short version.</strong> Independent UK carp gear reviews. Paid for by Amazon commissions on links you click. Ratings
        reflect what we would buy with our own money. That is it.
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
